  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d16099ea739ef4aa1993af1cac6a930f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Case01_AIImageCredibility
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ETEC510.Cases.CaseData
  CaseId: case01_ai_image
  Title: 'Case 01: Is This Image Real?'
  IntroVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 858d9dff77ce34244939d39bc8a48f9a, type: 3}
  IntroVideoFile: StartUpVideoNoAudio.mp4
  IntroMusic: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 318c0d06c94384739b0d58a2ab1ab4a2, type: 3}
  NarrationVideoFiles:
  - 1) Intro Video.mp4
  - 2) Badge 1 Intro.mp4
  - 6) Pragmatic Decision Point.mp4
  - 09) Badge 2 Intro.mp4
  - 14) Badge 3 IntroSplit.mov
  - 15) Badge 3 Decision.mp4
  - 17) Conclusion.mp4
  MainMusic: {fileID: 8300000, guid: dc987ed1832a54bb59c66d5aff5d76cb, type: 3}
  BriefingVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 12857437f439a47bbb0dfadc1f694faa, type: 3}
  BriefingVideoFile: 1) Intro Video.mp4
  BriefingLoopVideoFile: MissionBriefing.mp4
  BriefingText: "A photo of a protest has gone viral. Thousands of people are sharing
    it\u2014but something feels off.\n\nYou're the Lead Detective. Your mission:
    investigate this image and decide whether it's trustworthy before it spreads
    any further. Collect three clues to unlock the evidence vault, then deliver your
    verdict."
  BriefingImage: {fileID: 0}
  BriefingAudio: {fileID: 0}
  MissionStartVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: a40bb40b424394b3fa783919ab683b9b, type: 3}
  MissionStartVideoFile: 2) Badge 1 Intro.mp4
  EvidenceBoardImage: {fileID: 0}
  EvidenceBoardIntroVideo: {fileID: 0}
  EvidenceBoardIntroVideoFile: 
  SpotTheClueVideo: {fileID: 0}
  SpotTheClueVideoFile: 
  SpotTheClueBadgeVideoFile: 'BadgeCodeReveal-Pragmatic.mp4  '
  SpotTheClue:
    Prompt: 'LOOK CLOSELY at the image.


      AI-generated images often hide a
      tell-tale flaw. Can you find the visual glitch that gives it away?


      Which
      of these is the most obvious sign that this image is AI-generated?'
    EvidenceImage: {fileID: 0}
    Audio: {fileID: 0}
    Options:
    - Police lights inside
    - The colours look too bright
    CorrectIndex: 0
    FeedbackCorrect: 'Nice detective work! This image is different from normal. That''s
      Clue 1: the visual glitch.'
    FeedbackIncorrect: Look more carefully. Bright colours can appear in real photos
      too. Focus on the lights. Something isn't right there.
    CodeDigit: 5
  GutCheckBadgeVideoFile: BadgeCodeReveal-Dispositional.mp4
  DispositionalAwardVideoFile: 12) Badge 2 Award.mp4
  GutCheck:
    Prompt: 'Before sharing this image, what is your GUT REACTION?


      Does the
      scene feel realistic? Is the lighting consistent?


      What''s your verdict
      right now?'
    EvidenceImage: {fileID: 0}
    Audio: {fileID: 0}
    Options:
    - It looks real to me
    - "Something feels off \u2014 probably AI"
    CorrectIndex: 1
    FeedbackCorrect: "Good instinct! The background artefacts are giveaways. Trusting
      your gut \u2014 then verifying \u2014 is a key media-literacy skill."
    FeedbackIncorrect: Look again. The background details blur or repeat. AI generators
      often produce images that feel 'clean' in a way real photos don't.
    CodeDigit: 1
  FindTheMotiveBadgeVideoFile: 
  FindTheMotive:
    Prompt: "WHO would create and spread this image \u2014 and WHY?\n\nThink about:
      Who benefits if people believe this protest happened (or didn't)? What emotion
      is this image designed to trigger?\n\nWhat is the most likely motive behind
      this image?"
    EvidenceImage: {fileID: 0}
    Audio: {fileID: 0}
    Options:
    - To manipulate public opinion
    - To share an accurate news story
    CorrectIndex: 0
    FeedbackCorrect: "Exactly. Whoever made this image wanted to stir strong emotions
      \u2014 possibly to make a situation look worse. That's disinformation: fake
      visuals used to shape what people believe. Always ask: Who benefits from me
      believing this?"
    FeedbackIncorrect: "Think again. A real news story would use a verified photograph
      with a source and date. An AI-generated image has no original source \u2014
      it was created to mislead, not inform."
    CodeDigit: 0
  CriticalDecisionVideoFile: 6) Pragmatic Decision Point.mp4
  CriticalDecision:
    Options:
    - Analyze Account
    - Evaluate Comments
    - Extract Meta Data
    CorrectIndex: 2
    FeedbackCorrect: Good call! Checking the metadata is the most reliable way to
      verify an image's origin. Metadata reveals the device, date, location, and
      software used to create or edit a file.
    FeedbackIncorrect: Not quite. Try another approach to verify this image.
    BadgeVideoFile: 7) Pragmatic Badge Award.mp4
  Badge2IntroVideoFile: 09) Badge 2 Intro.mp4
  Badge3IntroVideoFile: 14) Badge 3 IntroSplit.mov
  Badge3DecisionVideoFile: 15) Badge 3 Decision.mp4
  Badge3DecisionFalseVideoFile: Badge3DecisionFalse.mp4
  Badge3AwardVideoFile: 16) Badge 3 Award.mp4
  ConclusionVideoFile: 17) Conclusion.mp4
  Password: 510
  UnlockVideo: {fileID: 0}
  UnlockVideoFile: 
  VaultEntryVideoFile: VaultEntry.mp4
  Verdict:
    Prompt: 'You''ve collected all three clues.


      Visual glitch

      Gut
      check

      Motive identified'
    EvidenceImage: {fileID: 0}
    Audio: {fileID: 0}
    Options:
    - REAL
    - FAKE
    CorrectIndex: 1
    FeedbackCorrect: "Case closed! You correctly identified this as an AI-generated
      image. Your three clues \u2014 the visual artefact, your gut check, and the
      motive \u2014 all pointed to the same conclusion. That's critical thinking
      in action."
    FeedbackIncorrect: 'Not quite. Review the clues: unidentified faces, the lighting,
      and the clear motive to manipulate all point to AI generation. Head back to
      the Chief for a hint.'
  HintVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: f37b4e5e9877f4ac9a94ab8bfb0f5860, type: 3}
  HintVideoFile: HintFromChief.mp4
  HintsOverlayVideoFile: HintsVideo.mp4
  HintText: "Listen up, Detective.\n\nThree questions to ask ANY suspicious image:\n\n1.
    Can I find this image somewhere credible with a date and source?\n2. Do the physical
    details (hands, shadows, text) look right?\n3. What strong emotion is this image
    trying to make me feel \u2014 and who gains from that reaction?\n\nNow go back
    and look again."
  HintImage: {fileID: 0}
  HintAudio: {fileID: 0}
  CompletionText: 'Outstanding detective work!


    You spotted the visual glitch,
    trusted your gut, identified the motive, and delivered the correct verdict.


    Remember:
    Before sharing any image, take 30 seconds to check the source, look for artefacts,
    and ask who benefits. That''s how misinformation stops spreading.'
  CompletionImage: {fileID: 0}
  CompletionAudio: {fileID: 0}
  XpForCompletion: 100
